.TH CERTWHY 1
.SH NAME
certwhy \- inspect a live TLS peer certificate and validation result
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B certwhy
--address HOST:PORT [--servername NAME] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to a TLS peer, validates its certificate chain, and reports certificate
identity, validity interval, SHA-256 fingerprint, negotiated TLS version, and
cipher suite. When validation fails but a diagnostic connection succeeds, the
certificate details are marked unverified; this never makes validation pass.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --address HOST:PORT
TLS endpoint. IPv6 addresses must use bracketed host:port syntax.
.TP
.B --servername NAME
TLS server name used for SNI and certificate validation; defaults to the host
part of --address.
.TP
.B --format json
Emit the versioned JSON report (the only supported format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means certificate validation passed; 1 means validation or connection failed;
2 invalid usage; and 4 a runtime failure.
